    <span class="cat-badge">Guide &middot; Rentals</span>
    <h1>Hanoi Motorbike Rental: Digital Nomads Rental Paperwork Questions</h1>
    <p>Digital nomads rent for the long middle of the calendar, and the paperwork for a working month is the paperwork of a relationship rather than a transaction. The questions to ask before signing are the ones that decide whether the rental survives its own length: monthly terms, renewal cycles, deposit mechanics, damage rules and what happens when the stay extends or shrinks. This page lists them for the nomad profile, and like every page in this cluster it invents no policy, quotes no rule the agreement has not written, and treats the counter conversation as the only source of rental truth.</p>
    <p>The page is part of the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental/">Hanoi motorbike rental</a> cluster, written for digital nomads. The verified fleet prices, including the monthly tier, are on the <a href="/hanoi-motorbike-rental-cost/">cost hub</a>, the general question bank is on the <a href="/faq/">FAQ</a> page, and the long-stay mechanics are expanded in the <a href="/monthly-motorbike-rental-hanoi/">monthly rental hub</a>.</p>

    <nav class="toc" aria-label="Table of contents">
      <p>On this page</p>
      <ol>
        <li><a href="#sec-1">Paperwork for a working month</a></li>
        <li><a href="#sec-2">The monthly agreement: what to confirm</a></li>
        <li><a href="#sec-3">Renewal and extension questions</a></li>
        <li><a href="#sec-4">Deposit mechanics for long stays</a></li>
        <li><a href="#sec-5">Damage, maintenance and the shop's half</a></li>
